        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(vault): aggregate provider outage diagnostics",
        "body": "Closes #110859\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using Vault-backed SecretRefs would receive one repeated provider-authentication diagnostic per affected owner during a shared Vault bootstrap or authentication outage, obscuring the common cause and producing noisy startup reports.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nVault resolution now distinguishes provider-wide bootstrap, explicit authentication, transport, and availability failures from path-specific reference failures. Runtime startup carries provider provenance internally and emits one provider diagnostic with the complete affected-owner list, including web-search/fetch owners, while preserving per-reference isolation for ACL failures, ambiguous 403 responses, failed token-introspection probes, and mixed batches. Bounded response parsing does not expose values or reference identifiers.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDuring an unambiguous Vault/provider outage, operators now see one actionable `SECRETS_PROVIDER_DEGRADED` diagnostic per failed provider and the affected owners. Path-specific permission failures remain isolated even when `lookup-self` is denied or temporarily unavailable, and mixed success/failure batches retain usable values.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Real Gateway outage proof: actual Vault resolver wrapper, model-provider, TTS, and web-search owners attributed to one failed provider; `/readyz` HTTP 200.\n- Real Gateway ACL proof: actual Vault resolver wrapper, two path 403 failures, denied `lookup-self`, owner-scoped warnings, no provider-failure provenance, and `/readyz` HTTP 200.\n- Final focused proof: Vault resolver 27/27, provider fan-out 4/4, and real Gateway owner-isolation 11/11 passed.\n- Remote proof: 91 focused tests passed across Vault resolution, runtime fan-out/warnings, and Gateway startup diagnostics/owner isolation.\n- Full Testbox gate: `pnpm check:changed` passed on the final source tree: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29659393543\n- Exact-head hosted CI: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29660352647\n- Fresh autoreview of the web-owner repair and test relocation: no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nAI-assisted implementation. I reviewed the behavior, tests, upstream Vault token-policy contract, and resulting diff.\n",
